BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 318 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 303 Td (- Resist offering solutions straight away) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 288 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 273 Td (The instinct of many managers is to jump to solutions. In a well-being conversation,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 258 Td (that can feel dismissive. Instead, let the person finish. Reflect back what you heard,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 243 Td (for example, it sounds like the workload has been weighing on you. Ask whether they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 228 Td (would like advice, or just to be heard. Silence is fine. When people feel listened to,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 213 Td (they often work out their own next step. If a practical change is needed, such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 198 Td (adjusting a deadline, you can agree it together once they have said what they need.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 0.25 0.25 0.27 rg 56 183 Td () Tj ET
